# Make a human paladin of Erich and get into the dungeon.
#
# There is no paladin among the other chargen scripts, and Zeal is a paladin
# spell, so tools/keys/zeal-strike.keys needs this one. It is built the same
# way as chargen-priest.keys -- by name where a name is on screen, by loop
# where the number of questions follows the seed -- for the same reason: a
# fixed stream of letters cannot answer a question that is only sometimes
# asked, and the letter beside an entry moves when the list above it changes.
#
# THE ORDER THE GAME ASKS IN, measured on seed 4:
#
#   race                 Human
#   racial skill x2      Human alone gets to name two skills as racial ones
#                        (see the race screen: "They may choose any two
#                        skills to treat as racial skills"), so this pair of
#                        prompts does not appear for any other race.
#   class                Paladin
#   god                  asked here, not after the skills as it is for a
#                        priest, because the paladin class is CF_RELIGIOUS
#                        and the game settles the god before the attributes.
#                        Erich because Zeal's own Desc says the spell "finds
#                        great favour with the paladins who serve Erich".
#   attributes           the first of the offered sets
#   alignment            the first offered; the class is CF_GOOD | CF_LAWFUL,
#                        so the game offers Lawful Good and little else
#   feats                a human paladin gets three at first level, so this
#                        is a loop rather than three letters
#   skill ranks          one pool
#   personality          colour only
#
# The trailing ESC dismisses the room description box that the game puts up
# on arrival ("Entry Chamber ... your first sight of the goblin caves").
# Without it the next key in the caller's script is eaten dismissing the box,
# and everything after it is off by one. Measured: with the ESC removed, the
# 'w' meant for wizard mode dismissed the box instead and the following 'y'
# opened the Yuse verb menu, because command keys are matched without regard
# to case and KY_CMD_YUSE is 'Y'.
#
# NOTE the paladin arrives with his sacred mount standing beside him -- a 'q'
# immediately west of the '@' on seed 4. A caller that wants an empty square
# next to the player must not assume west is free.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Human"
@choose "Athletics"      # first racial skill
@choose "Diplomacy"      # second racial skill
@choose "Paladin"
@choose "Erich"

a       # Attributes: the first of the offered sets
a       # Alignment:  the first offered

@while "Choose a feat" a

# Skill Manager. RIGHT spends a rank on the selected skill and stops at that
# skill's maximum; DOWN moves to the next skill. The loop matches the stars
# that count unspent ranks, not the header, which stays on screen when the
# pool is empty and so would never become false.
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

@while "wish to worship" y
@while "personality archetype" a

ESC     # dismiss the arrival room description
